Rhoform benchmark (b) — input-corner evidence.

Separate from validation.log because these are runs of MODIFIED decks, and the
transcript check in check-assertions.py holds validation.log to a fresh run of
the deck as shipped. Mixing them made the corner values look like drift.

Each block declares the single substitution that produced it, as
`# rerun: <old line> -> <new line>`. tests/benchmarks/check-corners.py applies
that edit to netlist.cir, runs it, and compares. So these numbers are evidence
that can be re-derived, not numbers in a file.

# rerun: V3 in 0 PWL(0 0 20u 0 220u 12 1 12) -> V3 in 0 PWL(0 0 20u 0 220u 9 1 9)
